# Intentionally almost empty.
#
# There used to be a catch-all here:
#
#   /*    /index.html   200
#
# which rewrote every unmatched path to the homepage and answered 200. That was
# needed while the app was a client-rendered SPA, but it meant /sitemap.xml,
# /assets/typo.js and every mistyped URL all looked like valid pages to a
# crawler — soft 404s across the entire site.
#
# Now that `postbuild` prerenders one real HTML file per route, Cloudflare Pages
# serves those files directly and answers 404 (with dist/404.html) for anything
# else, which is what a crawler should see. If the prerender ever fails, the
# build fails with it, so a half-built dist/ never reaches production.
#
# Add redirects here when URLs move, e.g.:
#   /old-path    /nuevo-path    301
